<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · city</p><h1 class="enc-title">Middelburg</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Middelburg is the capital of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/dutch">Dutch</a> province of Zeeland, on the former island of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/walcheren">Walcheren</a>. It grew around a fortified site and an abbey in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/middle-ages">Middle Ages</a> and became a leading trading town, the chief town of the county of Zeeland and later the seat of a chamber of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/dutch-east-india-company">Dutch East India Company</a>. Its town hall and abbey were rebuilt after German bombing in 1940.</p></div>
